{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795776383,"nonce":"e4NdHqQWfKFy1n7hBcW342BJRCA=","title":"A glass or blur image placeholder shows its tint in a group, a motion container or a 3D layer","message":"An image the frame draws itself puts its glass placeholder among the frame's glass. The others show the tint:\n\n- Inside a parent with opacity, a filter or a blend mode, the image is prepared as a batch of its own and inserted into the parent's stream. The insertion carries primitives and images, not glass. A LayerCommand::Glass would need the parent's group paint, which that batch does not have.\n- Inside a motion container or a 3D layer, the image is drawn after the frame's glass pass, with no backdrop.\n\nAn image with its own opacity below 1 and no group draws its placeholder glass at full strength, as GpuGlassPrimitive carries no opacity. At opacity 0 nothing is drawn.","files":null}]}